WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.617
This example compares individual source rows with their aggregated total.

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:09.247
Before aggregation, we can see each transaction separately.

00:00:09.247 --> 00:00:14.467
After aggregation, we see one combined product and month value.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:22.357
The total may be perfectly correct, but the individual transaction details cannot be recovered from that total alone.

00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:25.829
That is what information loss through aggregation means.
